 ],
 "seatAnchorNote": "seat is the painted cyan centroid. frontLegY is where that chair's front legs meet the floor, taken from the bottom of its blob in that column, so the bench's three slots each get their own because it runs diagonally. frontEdge is the front lip of the seat surface, one seat height above the legs, and it is where a seated sprite's knee belongs. ground stays for reference but nothing anchors to it: a sit pose's feet are wherever the drawing put them."
